//? Title: Interpolation Search: Exact Predictions and Actual Probe Histories
//? Subtitle: Uniform spacing, skew, duplicates and full signed-range arithmetic
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Find an integer key in a nondecreasing array by predicting its index from the
values at the current endpoints. The prediction can be exact for equally spaced
values and poor for skewed values. We preserve the original uniform and skewed
examples, inspect actual closed intervals, prove progress and exhibit a linear
worst-case family. Exact integer arithmetic fixes signed-overflow and floating
floor-boundary problems. Logical probes, endpoint tests, distribution
assumptions and sortedness preconditions are kept distinct.
)
\toc

> Start with a hand-checkable prediction

For [1,3,…,19] and key 13, the interval is [0,9], its endpoint values are one
and nineteen, and the exact offset is floor((13−1)·9/(19−1))=6. The first
candidate is therefore index six, whose value is thirteen. This deterministic
one-probe example is about equal spacing, not an observed random-data average.
The diagram uses the actual recorded interval and candidate from the search.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/interpolation_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/interpolation_search_analysis.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/binary_search.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    const auto a = dm::algorithms::interpolation_example_values();
    const auto t = dm::algorithms::interpolation_search_trace(a, 13);
    const auto &p = t.probes.front();
    std::print("| lo | hi | numerator | denominator | exact offset | actual index | actual value |\n| ---: " "| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",
               p.lo, p.hi, p.numerator, p.denominator, p.offset, p.position,
               p.value);
    std::print("Logical probes {}, endpoint tests {}, candidate tests {}.\n",
               t.run.result.probes, t.run.work.endpoint_guards,
               t.run.work.key_comparisons);
    dm::algorithms::interpolation_probe_diagram(t).save_svg(
        "build/interpolation_tiny.svg");
}
```
